{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts how many times a rotated binary string's integer value is odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(binary_string)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    # A binary number is odd if its least significant bit (rightmost digit) is '1'.\n    # When performing 'i' left circular shifts on the original string,\n    # the character that ends up at the last position (index n-1)\n    # is the character that was originally at index (i + n - 1) % n.\n    for i in range(rotations):\n        # Determine the original index of the character that will be the rightmost bit\n        # after 'i' left circular shifts.\n        effective_original_index = (i + n - 1) % n\n        \n        # Check if this character is '1', which signifies an odd number.\n        if binary_string[effective_original_index] == '1':\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds common elements in a list of lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Convert the first sublist to a set to initialize the common elements\n    common_elements = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the sublists and find intersections\n    for sublist in nested_lists[1:]:\n        common_elements.intersection_update(set(sublist))\n\n    return common_elements"}
