{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "import collections\ndef max_occurrences(items: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the item with the maximum frequency in a given list.\n    Returns None if the list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not items:\n        return None\n\n    counts = collections.Counter(items)\n    max_count = 0\n    max_item = None\n\n    for item, count in counts.items():\n        if count > max_count:\n            max_count = count\n            max_item = item\n        # If there's a tie, the item encountered first (due to Counter's iteration order\n        # or dictionary behavior) will be returned. The requirement doesn't specify\n        # tie-breaking, so this implicit behavior is acceptable.\n\n    return max_item"}
