{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "from typing import Tuple, Optional\ndef _extended_gcd(a: int, b: int) -> Tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes gcd(a, b) and coefficients x, y such that ax + by = gcd(a, b).\n    Returns (gcd, x, y).\n    \"\"\"\n    if b == 0:\n        return (a, 1, 0)\n\n    g, x_prime, y_prime = _extended_gcd(b, a % b)\n    x = y_prime\n    y = x_prime - (a // b) * y_prime\n    return (g, x, y)\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> Optional[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns integers x and y that satisfy ax + by = n as a tuple,\n    or return None if no solution exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return (0, 0) if n == 0 else None\n\n    g, x0, y0 = _extended_gcd(a, b)\n\n    # Ensure g (gcd) is positive and adjust x0, y0 accordingly.\n    if g < 0:\n        g = -g\n        x0 = -x0\n        y0 = -y0\n\n    if n % g != 0:\n        return None\n    \n    # Scale the particular solution (x0, y0) to satisfy ax + by = n.\n    k = n // g\n    x = x0 * k\n    y = y0 * k\n    \n    return (x, y)"}
