{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "import bisect\ndef is_majority(arr, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the index of the first occurrence of the element\n    first_idx = bisect.bisect_left(arr, element)\n\n    # If the element is not found or is out of bounds\n    if first_idx == n or arr[first_idx] != element:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the index of the last occurrence of the element\n    # bisect_right returns an insertion point which is one beyond the last occurrence\n    last_idx = bisect.bisect_right(arr, element) - 1\n\n    # Calculate the count of the element\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    # Check if the count is greater than n/2\n    return count > n / 2"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(n):\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of set bits (1s) in the binary representation of a number using Brian Kernighan's algorithm.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    # Use 0xFFFFFFFF to handle negative numbers by taking their 32-bit two's complement representation.\n    # For positive numbers within 32 bits, this mask doesn't change their value.\n    value = n & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    while value:\n        value &= (value - 1)\n        count += 1\n    return count"}
