{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "import collections\ndef check_occurences(list_of_tuples):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the occurrences of unique unordered tuples in a list.\n\n    Inner classes TuplePair and OccurrenceCounter facilitate the processing\n    by normalizing tuples and aggregating counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    class TuplePair:\n        def __init__(self, a, b):\n            self.first = a\n            self.second = b\n\n        def sorted(self):\n            # Returns a new TuplePair with elements arranged in ascending order.\n            return TuplePair(min(self.first, self.second), max(self.first, self.second))\n\n        def __hash__(self):\n            # Enables TuplePair instances to be used as dictionary keys.\n            return hash((self.first, self.second))\n\n        def __eq__(self, other):\n            # Defines equality for TuplePair instances.\n            if not isinstance(other, TuplePair):\n                return NotImplemented\n            return self.first == other.first and self.second == other.second\n\n    class OccurrenceCounter:\n        def __init__(self):\n            self.counts = collections.defaultdict(int)\n\n        def add(self, p: TuplePair):\n            # Increments the count for the given normalized TuplePair.\n            self.counts[p] += 1\n\n        def get_counts(self):\n            # Converts internal TuplePair keys back to standard Python tuples.\n            result = {}\n            for tp_key, count in self.counts.items():\n                result[(tp_key.first, tp_key.second)] = count\n            return result\n\n    counter = OccurrenceCounter()\n    for item_tuple in list_of_tuples:\n        # Create a TuplePair from the input, then normalize it by sorting.\n        tuple_pair = TuplePair(item_tuple[0], item_tuple[1])\n        sorted_tuple_pair = tuple_pair.sorted()\n        counter.add(sorted_tuple_pair)\n\n    return counter.get_counts()"}
