{"task_id": "Mbpp/287", "solution": "class EvenNumberSequence:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates logic to generate even numbers, square them, and sum the results.\n    Attributes store intermediate lists of even numbers and their squares.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, n: int):\n        self.n = n\n        self.even_numbers = []\n        self.squares = []\n        self.sum = 0\n\n    def calculate(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Generates the first n even natural numbers, squares them, and calculates their sum.\n        The result is stored in the 'sum' attribute and also returned.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self.n <= 0:\n            return 0\n\n        for i in range(1, self.n + 1):\n            self.even_numbers.append(2 * i)\n\n        for num in self.even_numbers:\n            self.squares.append(num * num)\n\n        self.sum = sum(self.squares)\n        return self.sum\ndef square_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of the squares of the first n even natural numbers.\n    It leverages the EvenNumberSequence class for the core calculation logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    calculator = EvenNumberSequence(n)\n    return calculator.calculate()"}
