{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "def min_val(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum numeric value in a heterogeneous list, ignoring non-numeric elements.\n    Returns None if no numeric values are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_found = None\n    for item in input_list:\n        try:\n            # Attempt a numeric operation to determine if 'item' is numeric.\n            # This will raise a TypeError for non-numeric types that don't support arithmetic operations.\n            _ = item + 0.0\n\n            # If the operation succeeded, 'item' is numeric.\n            if min_found is None:\n                min_found = item\n            elif item < min_found:\n                min_found = item\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            # If TypeError or ValueError occurs, 'item' is not a comparable numeric type.\n            # Ignore it and continue to the next item.\n            continue\n        except Exception:\n            # Catch any other unexpected exceptions during evaluation, still ignoring the item.\n            continue\n\n    return min_found"}
