{"task_id": "Mbpp/455", "solution": "class Month:\n    \"\"\"\n    Represents a month with its number and properties like the number of days.\n    Raises ValueError for invalid month numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, number: int):\n        if not 1 <= number <= 12:\n            raise ValueError(\"Month number must be between 1 and 12.\")\n        self.number = number\n        self.days = self._determine_days()\n\n    def _determine_days(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Determines the number of days for the month.\"\"\"\n        if self.number in {1, 3, 5, 7, 8, 10, 12}:\n            return 31\n        elif self.number in {4, 6, 9, 11}:\n            return 30\n        else: # February\n            return 28 # For the purpose of checking for 31 days, exact February days are not critical.\n\n    def has31Days(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the month has exactly 31 days.\"\"\"\n        return self.days == 31\ndef check_monthnumb_number(month_number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks whether the given month number contains 31 days.\n    Raises ValueError if the month number is invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    month_instance = Month(month_number)\n    return month_instance.has31Days()"}
