{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "def Find_Min(list_of_sublists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sublist with the minimum length from a list of sublists.\n    If multiple sublists have the same minimum length, the first one encountered is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_sublists:\n        # According to design, this should raise ValueError, but instructions say \"DO NOT raise exceptions for edge cases\".\n        # Assuming valid non-empty input as per assertion.\n        return None \n\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    min_sublist = None\n\n    for sublist in list_of_sublists:\n        # According to design, this should raise TypeError if elements are not lists, but instructions say \"DO NOT add isinstance() checks\".\n        # Assuming all elements are lists as per assertion.\n        current_length = len(sublist)\n        if current_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_length\n            min_sublist = sublist\n            \n    return min_sublist"}
