{"task_id": "Mbpp/555", "solution": "def difference(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the difference between sum of cubes and sum of first n natural numbers.\n    Uses closed-form formulas for O(1) complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    sum_n = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    sum_cubes_n = sum_n ** 2\n    return sum_cubes_n - sum_n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "import math\ndef find_Odd_Pair(numbers: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of unordered pairs of integers in a list whose bitwise XOR is odd.\n    A pair has an odd XOR if and only if one number is even and the other is odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(num, int):\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements in the input list must be integers.\")\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    return even_count * odd_count"}
