{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all lucid numbers (1 and prime numbers) up to a given integer n.\n    Returns an empty list if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    lucid_numbers = [1]\n\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime.\"\"\"\n        if num <= 1:\n            return False\n        if num <= 3:  # 2 and 3 are prime\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:  # Multiples of 2 or 3 are not prime\n            return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        if is_prime(i):\n            lucid_numbers.append(i)\n\n    return lucid_numbers"}
