{"task_id": "Mbpp/615", "solution": "def average_tuple(tuple_of_tuples):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the average value for each inner tuple in a tuple of tuples.\n    Returns a list of these averages.\n    \"\"\"\n    averages = []\n    for inner_tuple in tuple_of_tuples:\n        if inner_tuple: # Ensure the inner tuple is not empty to avoid ZeroDivisionError\n            averages.append(sum(inner_tuple) / len(inner_tuple))\n        else:\n            # Based on the prompt, assume valid input and no empty inner tuples\n            # If empty tuples were allowed, a choice would be needed: 0, None, or raise error\n            pass \n    return averages"}
