{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "def pair_xor_Sum(numbers, n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of XOR of all unique pairs in the first n elements of the list.\n    Returns 0 if n < 2 or the list is empty.\"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n\n    if n < 2 or not numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    # Iterate over all unique unordered pairs among the first n elements\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            total_sum += (numbers[i] ^ numbers[j])\n\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of numbers using the heap sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list without modifying the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = list(lst)  # Create a mutable copy of the input list\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    def _heapify(arr, n, i):\n        \"\"\"Helper function to maintain the max-heap property.\"\"\"\n        largest = i\n        left = 2 * i + 1\n        right = 2 * i + 2\n\n        if left < n and arr[i] < arr[left]:\n            largest = left\n\n        if right < n and arr[largest] < arr[right]:\n            largest = right\n\n        if largest != i:\n            arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]\n            _heapify(arr, n, largest)\n\n    # Build a maxheap from the input array\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one from the heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]  # Swap current root with last element\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)  # Call heapify on the reduced heap\n\n    return arr"}
