{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a given list by a specified number of items to the right.\n    The rotation is performed on a copy, leaving the original list unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    list_len = len(input_list)\n    if list_len == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Normalize n to be within the range [0, list_len - 1]\n    n_effective = n % list_len\n\n    # Perform the rotation using list slicing\n    return input_list[-n_effective:] + input_list[:-n_effective]"}
