{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "def jacobsthal_num(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Jacobsthal number using an iterative approach.\n    Applies the recurrence J(n) = J(n-1) + 2*J(n-2) with J(0)=0 and J(1)=1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 0, 1  # Corresponds to J(0) and J(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, b + 2 * a\n    return b"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/754", "solution": "def extract_index_list(l1, l2, l3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements that are common for lists l1, l2, l3 if they appear in all three lists under the same index.\n    Returns a list of such common elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    common_elements = []\n    min_length = min(len(l1), len(l2), len(l3))\n\n    for i in range(min_length):\n        if l1[i] == l2[i] and l2[i] == l3[i]:\n            common_elements.append(l1[i])\n            \n    return common_elements"}
