{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Assumes the input array `arr` is already sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find further occurrences in the right half\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
