{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number, d):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit number to the left by d positions.\n    The rotation wraps around the 32-bit boundary.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_bits = 32\n    d = d % num_bits\n    return ((number << d) | (number >> (num_bits - d))) & ((1 << num_bits) - 1)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "import math\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, k, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in an array repeated k times.\n    The parameter 'n' is included in the signature as per requirements, but the core\n    logic finds the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray of any length, aligning with\n    the provided assertion example.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    def kadane(nums):\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray of any length.\n        Handles arrays with all negative numbers by correctly identifying the largest\n        single element as the maximum sum in such cases.\n        \"\"\"\n        max_so_far = -math.inf\n        current_max = 0\n        max_val_in_array = -math.inf # To track the largest single element, for all-negative arrays\n\n        for x in nums:\n            max_val_in_array = max(max_val_in_array, x) # Keep track of the maximum single element\n            current_max += x\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n            if current_max < 0:\n                current_max = 0\n        \n        # If all subarray sums (resetting negatives) resulted in 0 or less,\n        # and the largest individual element is negative, then the actual max sum\n        # for a non-empty subarray is that largest individual element.\n        # This condition is typically true when max_so_far will be <= 0 and max_val_in_array < 0.\n        if max_so_far <= 0 and max_val_in_array < 0:\n            return max_val_in_array\n        \n        return max_so_far\n\n    # 1. Calculate the maximum subarray sum within a single instance of `arr`.\n    max_sum_single = kadane(arr)\n\n    # 2. Calculate the total sum of `arr`.\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n\n    # 3. Calculate the maximum sum of any prefix of `arr`.\n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    max_prefix_val = -math.inf\n    for x in arr:\n        current_prefix_sum += x\n        max_prefix_val = max(max_prefix_val, current_prefix_sum)\n\n    # 4. Calculate the maximum sum of any suffix of `arr`.\n    current_suffix_sum = 0\n    max_suffix_val = -math.inf\n    for i in range(len(arr) - 1, -1, -1):\n        x = arr[i]\n        current_suffix_sum += x\n        max_suffix_val = max(max_suffix_val, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    # If the array is repeated only once, the answer is just the max sum within `arr`.\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_sum_single\n    else:\n        # For k > 1, consider subarrays that span across multiple repetitions.\n        # This includes a suffix of the first array, (k-2) full repetitions of arr\n        # (if k > 2, otherwise 0), and a prefix of the last array.\n        # We only add `total_sum` if it's positive, otherwise, it detracts from the max sum.\n        middle_blocks_sum = max(0, total_sum) * (k - 2)\n        \n        # The maximum sum for a subarray spanning multiple blocks is the sum of:\n        # - The best possible suffix sum from the first `arr`\n        # - The sum of `k-2` full `arr` blocks (if positive)\n        # - The best possible prefix sum from the last `arr`\n        max_spanning_sum = max_prefix_val + middle_blocks_sum + max_suffix_val\n        \n        # The overall maximum sum is the greater of a subarray contained entirely\n        # within a single `arr` instance, or a subarray spanning multiple `arr` instances.\n        return max(max_sum_single, max_spanning_sum)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/430", "solution": "def parabola_directrix(a: float, b: float, c: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the y-coordinate of the directrix for a parabola y = ax^2 + bx + c.\n    Raises ValueError if coefficient 'a' is zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Coefficient a must be non-zero.\")\n    return c - (b**2 + 1) / (4 * a)"}
